{"content":"⚠️ **IMPORTANT: The fixed path has no automated regression coverage**

Moving `QuickjsRuntime()` inside the try is the actual fix, but nothing in CI can detect a regression of it. The only related test (`dispatch/wait roundtrip without a JS engine on the caller`, `test/js/async_job_pool_test.dart:289`) asserts `envelope.ok isTrue` — it passes with or without this fix on any machine where the dylib exists, and CI always has a working dylib. So if the boot ever moves back outside the try, every gate stays green and the infinite hang returns.

A deterministic test is feasible without hiding the dylib, because `quickjs_ffi.dart` honors `JSR_QUICKJS_LIB` unconditionally when set (`_resolveLibraryPath` returns it before any existence check). Spawn a child process so the parent test run keeps its working engine:

```dart
test('worker boot failure (missing dylib) fails fast per job', () async {
  final harness = File('${Directory.systemTemp.path}/hang_probe.dart')
    ..writeAsStringSync('''
import 'package:dmtools/src/js/async_job_pool.dart';
Future<void> main() async {
  final pool = AsyncJobPool(workers: 1);
  await pool.boot();
  final id = pool.dispatch(
    fnSource: 'function(args) { return 1; }',
    argsJson: '[]',
    scriptDirectory: Directory.systemTemp.path,
    params: const {},
  );
  final envelope = pool.wait(id);
  print('OK=\${envelope.ok} ERR=\${envelope.error}');
  pool.dispose();
}
''');
  final result = await Process.run(
    Platform.resolvedExecutable,
    ['run', harness.path],
    environment: {'JSR_QUICKJS_LIB': '/nonexistent/libquickjs_bridge.so'},
  ).timeout(const Duration(seconds: 60)); // pre-fix: this times out (hang)
  expect(result.stdout, contains('OK=false'));
  expect(result.stdout, contains('DynamicLibrary.open')); // clear cause
});
```

I verified during this review that with the fix in place the scenario completes in ~2s with `ok:false`; on `origin/main` it hangs until killed. (AGENTS.md §1.5: tests ship with code — the hang is the bug this PR exists for, so it deserves a permanent tripwire.)
